        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Hume Auctioneers - We Get The Pick Of The Crop.\n\nThe Green is a beautiful enclave of quality homes, designed for over 55s.\n\nSet around a beautiful green area, the development offers a relaxed atmosphere where homes are maintained to a beautiful standard.\n\nNo. 53 is particularly attractive being a detached property set on a large corner site with excellent and spacious parking.\n\nThe interior is bright, spacious and exceptionally well laid out, with all accommodation arranged on one convenient level.\n\nA welcoming entrance hall, finished with attractive timber flooring and decorative ceiling coving, leads to a generously proportioned living room. This comfortable, light-filled reception space enjoys windows on two sides and features timber flooring, an attractive fireplace and double doors opening directly to the kitchen/dining room.\n\nExtending to approximately 5.49 metres, the kitchen/dining room offers excellent space for everyday living and dining. The kitchen is fitted with an extensive range of solid timber-style units, generous worktop space, tiled splashbacks, an integrated oven and gas hob, together with provision for both a washing machine and dishwasher.\n\n The spacious dining area enjoys abundant natural light, timber flooring and glazed French doors opening to the outside.\n\nThe large double bedroom is particularly well proportioned and benefits from its own private ensuite. \n\nA separate main bathroom is fitted with a full-sized bath, WC and wash-hand basin.\n\nThe second bedroom is also generously proportioned.\n\nOutside there is a small yard area with a good garden shed. The patio overlooks the green and offers a very pleasant outlook.\n\nKilminchy Village is a most sought-after neighbourhood. Designed by internationally renowned architect Melville Dunbar. \n\nKilminchy's design is based upon the highly regarded Essex town plan, which has been executed to a magnificent standard in this most convenient location and resembles the meandering streets of a small village or town. \n\nWithin the development is a neighbourhood centre to include, shops, restaurants, Pharmacy and a gastropub. The recreational amenities are excellent too and include natural lakes, a purpose-built basketball court and acres of green space. Schools, shops, leisure centre and the hospital are all within walking distance, whilst Portlaoise town centre and the M7 motorway are just a few minutes away by car. \n\nMidlands Hospital Portlaoise is just a few hundred metres away.\n\nThere is a magnificent hourly Bus service to Dublin which stops at the entrance, every hour day and night. The development has been prewired with fibre optic broadband cable and speeds of up to 1gb are available. \n\nNew Portlaoise Bus Route Stops At Entrance With Round The Clock Access To Train, Schools & Town Centre Viewing Highly Recommended."
      },
